Injecting into a json file can be quite tedious with regex alone.

Would be nice to be able to give a dot path instead of regex.

```ejs
---
inject: true
to: some/path.json
json_insert_path: '.foo.bar'
---
{
	"some": "value"
}

```

The resulting json would be
```json
{
	"foo": { 
		"bar" : {
			"some": "value"
		}
	}
}
```

And if you wanted to just insert at the root you could use `.` as the path

